From: Thadeu Lima de Souza Cascardo <cascardo@canonical.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xfrm6: free oversized packets on local PMTU errors

Backport upstream 215ab0f021c9fea3c18b75e7d522400ee6a49990
(xfrm6: call kfree_skb when skb is toobig) to the 3.10 skb-only API.
Both EMSGSIZE exits own the skb and must release its destination references.
Retain all PMTU error reporting, fragmentation, transform and policy checks.

Original Signed-off-by: Thadeu Lima de Souza Cascardo <cascardo@canonical.com>
Original Reviewed-by: Sabrina Dubroca <sd@queasysnail.net>
Original Signed-off-by: Steffen Klassert <steffen.klassert@secunet.com>
---
--- a/net/ipv6/xfrm6_output.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/xfrm6_output.c
@@ -140,9 +140,11 @@
 
 	if (skb->len > mtu && xfrm6_local_dontfrag(skb)) {
 		xfrm6_local_rxpmtu(skb, mtu);
+		kfree_skb(skb);
 		return -EMSGSIZE;
 	} else if (!skb->local_df && skb->len > mtu && skb->sk) {
 		xfrm6_local_error(skb, mtu);
+		kfree_skb(skb);
 		return -EMSGSIZE;
 	}
 
